On Tue, Apr 27, 2004 at 01:06:03PM -0500, Jeffrey Forman wrote:
> Hate to rain on everyone's apparent gcc/pie/ssp parade but Gentoo Linux
> 2004.1 is getting released to the world today/tomorrow, depending on
> your particular locale on the globe.

I'm happy to hear it.

I'm also sad, and regretful, that I was not able to get the promised Alpha
port done in time for this release. Between a paying job that got in the way
during the time that most folks were bulding 2004.1, and a con I'd committed
to go to a long time ago, and then dealing with the fallout from that (seen
the pictures of the guy in the TRON costume floating around the net? That's
me), I flat fell down on the job.

I feel like I let the side down. Hopefully, for 2004.2, I'll be able to do
the job I promised to do when I was accepted as a developer. In the
meantime, I'll at least get a 2004.1 experimental release set built; it'll
be useful even if it's not an official Gentoo release.

I'm really sorry, folks.

...Jay

